:2016,"v":44.0},{"s":2017,"v":44.4},{"s":2018,"v":57.2},{"s":2019,"v":53.7},{"s":2020,"v":45.3},{"s":2021,"v":31.3},{"s":2022,"v":71.8},{"s":2023,"v":43.3},{"s":2024,"v":22.1},{"s":2025,"v":50.6}],"t_snow":{"per_decade":1.128,"lo":0.51,"hi":1.747,"class":"signal","n":142,"first":1884,"last":2025,"intercept":-178.49309731323518,"slope":0.11282421504177574,"total":15.9},"snow_normal":51.5},"titles":{"year":"2026 so far: 11 daily record highs, no daily record lows","records":"Record highs keep coming. Record lows have nearly stopped.","change":"Madison's nights cooled over the long run but have warmed since 1986. Its days warmed over the long run.","rain":"Madison has gotten wetter"},"text":{"lede":"Yesterday's high of 42\u00b0F was typical for November 13.","t_yest":"November 13 was a typical day","p_yest":"The high of <strong>42\u00b0F</strong> was typical for November 13. The normal high for the date is 46\u00b0F, and the record is 69\u00b0F (1999). The low of <strong>27\u00b0F</strong> was typical for November 13.","t_rec":"Record highs keep coming. Record lows have nearly stopped.","p_rec":"If Madison's climate weren't changing, every year would have the same chance of holding a daily record. Since 2000, Madison has set <strong class=\"sig\">23 standing record lows</strong>, far fewer than the 62 that chance alone would give, and <strong class=\"sig\">99 record highs</strong>, far more than the 62 that chance alone would give. The 1950s hold the most record highs of any decade (43). Madison's all-time high is 107\u00b0F, on July 14, 1936.","t_chg":"Madison's nights cooled over the long run but have warmed since 1986. Its days warmed over the long run.","p_chg":"Across 157 complete years: Madison's average low has fallen <strong class='sig'>\u22120.11\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range \u22120.19 to \u22120.03), about \u22121.7\u00b0F since 1869. Madison's average high has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.32\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.26 to +0.39), about +5.1\u00b0F since 1869. <strong>The last 40 years tell a different story:</strong> since 1986, lows have risen <strong class='sig'>+0.68\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.23 to +1.12) and highs show no clear change. The full record joins different observing sites over the years, and a move (for example, from the city to a cooler airport) can hide or exaggerate a long-run trend, so the recent decades are the clearer guide here.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 1 of 12 months; 7 months fell. Highs rose in all 12 months.","t_rain":"Madison has gotten wetter","p_rain":"Madison's yearly precipitation has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.33 inches per decade</strong> (95% range +0.10 to +0.56), about +5.1 inches since 1869. The 1991\u20132020 normal is 37.1 inches a year. The wettest year was 1881 (52.91 in); the driest, 1895 (13.69 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":true,"hi":true},"t_year":"2026 so far: 11 daily record highs, no daily record lows"}}